loop 9 | Tool=Write, Args={"file_path": "/home/silimon/.claude/plans/peaceful-cooking-sparkle.md", "content": "# Set up Tailscale MCP Echo Server\n\n## Context\n\nInstall the `tailscale-mcp-echo` MCP server (GitHub: `remyguercio/tailscale-mcp-echo`). This is a FastMCP-based Python server that provides identity-aware functionality via Tailscale headers. Per the project rules, the server name is `983720150_remyguercio_tailscale-mcp-echo`.\n\n**Key constraint:** Docker and Tailscale are NOT available on this machine. The README's `docker compose up` approach won't work. Instead, we'll run the FastMCP server directly via `uv` with stdio transport. The `greet` tool will still be available, but Tailscale identity headers will be absent (returning \"Unknown\" for user info).\n\n## Steps\n\n### 1. Clone the repo\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p /home/silimon/mcp-auto/mcp_server/983720150_remyguercio_tailscale-mcp-echo\ngit clone https://github.com/remyguercio/tailscale-mcp-echo.git /home/silimon/mcp-auto/mcp_server/983720150_remyguercio_tailscale-mcp-echo\n```\n\n### 2. Create `.env` file with placeholder auth key\n\n```bash\necho \"TS_AUTHKEY=tskey-auth-placeholder\" > /home/silimon/mcp-auto/mcp_server/983720150_remyguercio_tailscale-mcp-echo/.env\n```\n\n### 3. Install Python dependencies\n\nThe project requires Python >=3.13 (`pyproject.toml`). uv will auto-download 3.13 if needed:\n\n```bash\ncd /home/silimon/mcp-auto/mcp_server/983720150_remyguercio_tailscale-mcp-echo\n/home/silimon/.local/bin/uv sync\n```\n\n### 4. Add MCP server configuration\n\nUse `add_config` tool with:\n- **name:** `983720150_remyguercio_tailscale-mcp-echo`\n- **type:** `stdio`\n- **command:** `/home/silimon/.local/bin/uv`\n- **args:** `[\"run\", \"main.py\", \"--transport\", \"stdio\"]`\n- **env:** `{\"MCP_TRANSPORT\": \"stdio\"}`\n- **cwd:** `/home/silimon/mcp-auto/mcp_server/983720150_remyguercio_tailscale-mcp-echo`\n\nThe `--transport stdio` flag tells FastMCP to use stdio instead of HTTP, which is required for MCP clients to communicate over stdin/stdout.\n\n### 5. Validate the configuration\n\nUse `validate_config` tool with name `983720150_remyguercio_tailscale-mcp-echo`.\n\nExpected outcome: the server starts via stdio, MCP-Auto connects, and the `greet` tool appears in the tool list.\n\n## Files to Modify\n\n- `/home/silimon/mcp-auto/mcp_server_config/config.json` — add server entry via `add_config` tool\n- `/home/silimon/mcp-auto/mcp_server/983720150_remyguercio_tailscale-mcp-echo/` — cloned repo + `.env`\n\n## Verification\n\n1. After `validate_config` reports success, confirm the `greet` tool is listed\n2. Note: the `greet` tool will return \"Unknown\" for user identity since no Tailscale proxy is running\n"}
